# 17. A pendulum as a CONSTRAINT, not a force.
# A rod is a geometric fact: the bob is exactly L from the pivot, always.
# Writing that as a stiff spring only approximates it. Writing it as an
# algebraic equation turns the problem into a DAE, which is what IDA is
# for. The small-amplitude period is T = 2*pi*sqrt(L/g).
set system.g_constant = 0
set system.uniform_gravity = [0, -9.81, 0]
collide off
# inverse_mass = 0 makes the pivot an ANCHOR: it never moves, and it
# absorbs the rod's reaction.
new sphere as pivot { mass = 1, radius = 0.02, position = [0, 0, 0], inverse_mass = 0 }
# start 0.02 rad off vertical, so the linear period applies
new sphere as bob { mass = 1, radius = 0.05, position = [0.019998666693333084, -0.9998000066665778, 0] }
# no length given: freeze the separation they already have
constrain pivot bob
constraints
method ida
# one small-amplitude period: 2*pi*sqrt(1/9.81)
run 2.0060666807106475 steps 200
get bob.position
constraints
